.TH ferry-config-set 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-config\-set \- Change one setting
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry config set\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change one setting
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
Setting name
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
device\-name: Name of this device visible to others
.IP \(bu 2
language: Interface language code
.IP \(bu 2
network\-mode: `local`, `internet`, `relay` or `relay\-only` (the relay modes need `relay\-urls`)
.IP \(bu 2
download\-dir: Folder for received files
.IP \(bu 2
hidden: Hidden on the local network from unpaired devices (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
paired\-only: Accept files, texts and pairing only from paired devices (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
strip\-metadata: Send photos (JPEG, PNG) without their location and other metadata (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
announce\-platform: Tell everyone on the local network which operating system this is (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
random\-port: Listen on a random port instead of the fixed 47824; applies at the next start (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
auto\-accept\-texts: Copy texts from Auto\-Accept devices without asking (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
auto\-accept\-executables: Accept programs, scripts and macro documents from Auto\-Accept devices without asking (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
quit\-on\-close: Desktop app: quit when the window is closed instead of staying in the tray (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
relay\-urls: Relays of the `relay` and `relay\-only` network modes, separated by commas (`https://relay.example.org`)
.IP \(bu 2
history: Keep a history of transfers (`true`/`false`)
.IP \(bu 2
speed\-limit: Speed limit for sending and, separately, receiving (`500K`, `2M`, `off`)
.IP \(bu 2
localsend: Receive files from LocalSend apps – iPhone, Mac – without pairing (`true`/`false`)
.RE
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
New value
